0},"meta":{"digest":"4d31d5c9b20e520fcb711ecc870e67e3eb8c2b7d78c2df3bc12854acc3314144","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5.1.1/meta.json","size_bytes":6010},"prompt":{"digest":"8975ecf7d76dd2d9b1ed1cce4249cbf873f2a458dd083968fafca4399e350873","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5.1.1/prompt.md","size_bytes":181},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"b7ac7fe2d96345e7b18b64202fa862a9507ea181df71de3e88cc3e3a02536ae6","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5.1.1/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":6987},"state":{"digest":"b9bec9564f87920245d3f1255053624bea8c7e63ffbe35f6674cd42beb152170","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5.1.1/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-11-04T12:16:47.841457+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5.1.1","local_name":"sase-1r5.1.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-1r5.1","agent_clan_generation":"20261104065640","bead_id":"sase-1r5.1.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-1r5.1[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Retry transient GitHub SSH publickey denials on git network [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]operations[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]A GitHub-side burst of `Permission denied (publickey)` rejections [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]of valid SSH keys no longer aborts agent launches or background git[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]jobs. Launch-blocking and background git network operations retry [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]such denials within a bounded, deadline-aware budget. Genuine [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]credential failures still surface promptly as permanent [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]authentication errors that keep the original stderr: deploy-key [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]refusals, a host with no local SSH credential at all, and a denial [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]that outlasts the budget.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]github_publickey_retry.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/github_publickey_retry.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1r5.1[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1r5/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]sase-1r5.1.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-core credential_unconfirmed verdict for SSH publickey [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]denials[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-verdict[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-verdict: in sase-core, classify SSH publickey denials on git and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]git_clone operations as a new non-retryable `credential_unconfirmed` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]verdict whose reason keeps the `authentication` category. Deploy-key [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]refusals stay permanent, the retryability module becomes a facade, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]table and parity tests cover the new verdict.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase pin bump and shared credential-confirmation retry policy[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]credential-retry-policy[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-verdict[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]credential-retry-policy: move sase's sase-core CI pin past the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]classifier change and add the Python wire constant. Add a shared, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]deadline-aware credential-retry tracker with launch and background [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]budgets, an env kill switch, a per-host exhaustion memo, and a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]conservative local-SSH-credential precheck that fails fast when no [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]credential exists.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt credential retries in the SDD store clone[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]sdd-clone-adopt[dim] · [dim][/dim]after credential-retry-policy[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sdd-clone-adopt: give `clone_sdd_store_to_path` a credential-retry [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]budget separate from its transient schedule, using the launch budget, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]never holding the clone admission permit while sleeping. Prove it with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]an SSH-shim fake GitHub remote that denies N times and then serves a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]real bare repo.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt credential retries in SDD network git and workspace [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]lease fetch[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]network-git-and-lease-adopt[dim] · [dim][/dim]after credential-retry-policy[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]network-git-and-lease-adopt: route publickey denials in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`run_sdd_network_git_with_retries` (agent publication) and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]operational-lease `git fetch` through the shared tracker, replacing the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lease's bespoke one-shot confirmation. Keep `is_credential_failure`, the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ssh-agent hint, and the external mirror's `auth_error` label intact.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Document the auth-retry behavior and record follow-ups[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs-and-followups[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sdd-clone-adopt, network-git-and-lease-adopt[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs-and-followups: document the retry budgets, kill switch, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fast-fail cases in the service-host and SDD docs. Note the deploy-key [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]marker on sase-167, record proposed follow-ups for network git sites [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that never consult the classifier, and run the shim end to end against [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]both adopted paths.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1r5.1","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1r5.1.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-025c9986d2efad00506feaa5a03acec1","started_at":"2026-11-04T11:57:30.495444+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"dda3bc998a708757e538af0e7f0f3a755b9085a770eed47e8a519e6340a5993e","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5.1.5/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"805b994699c7f7964d7fb2e8f924496bcee12197e9454762ee24482f5b9e18e0","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5.1.5/meta.json","size_bytes":702},"prompt":{"digest":"448e844cc8df68da6ee47140107f762b5fe1cc2c1792b3eaec91619fc175f56a","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5.1.5/prompt.md","size_bytes":207},"state":{"digest":"882708790ccb28489492fa1ee56bfbd9d1437aaad02ef0739d48d6f27ca3d32b","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5.1.5/state.json","size_bytes":163}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5.1.5","local_name":"sase-1r5.1.5","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-1r5.1","agent_clan_generation":"20261104065640","bead_id":"sase-1r5.1.5","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1r5.1","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1r5.1.5","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub","wait_for_beads":["sase-1r5.1.3","sase-1r5.1.4"]},"source_run_id":"run-046e